module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FreeSheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.QuotientRingSheafOpenSubspaceIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulResolutionOfIdealSheaf

/-!
# The ideal a Koszul morphism generates, read on the slice site

Let `X` be a ringed space, `U` an open of it and `f₁, …, f_r` sections of `O_X` over `U`. The
local statements of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] are formed on the restricted ringed space `X|_U`, where
the ideal in play is the one generated by
`Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulHomOfSections` of the `fᵢ` read as *global* sections there; the
gluing of those statements runs on the slice site `Opens X / U`, where the ideal in play is the
one generated by the restrictions of the `fᵢ` themselves.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` identifies the two quotients of the
structure sheaf over `U` provided the two sheaves of ideals have the same sections, and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspace` reduces that hypothesis, for
ideals generated by a morphism, to an *objectwise* agreement of the two images. **This file
supplies that objectwise agreement for the Koszul morphism**, which is the comparison the
gluing of the tag was left owing.

The two images are computed against one description: for a finite free sheaf of modules the
objectwise image of a morphism is the span of the images of the tautological sections
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_range_app_free_iff`), so both sides are the ideal generated by the
restrictions of `f₁, …, f_r` over the open in question. No slice-site free sheaf of modules, and
hence no sheafification over the slice site, is involved on the upstairs side: the ideal there is
written directly as the span of a family of sections.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.spanSections`: the submodule of a presheaf of modules generated,
  objectwise, by a finite family of its sections. Stability under restriction is the
  compatibility of the family.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sliceSections`: the family of sections of the
  slice structure sheaf `O_X|_U` given by `f₁, …, f_r`, namely their restrictions along the
  structure morphism of each object of `Opens X / U`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sliceIdealOfSections`: **the sheaf of ideals of
  `O_X|_U` generated by `f₁, …, f_r`**, the local closure of the previous span. This is the `I`
  that the identification of the two quotients consumes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_range_app_free_iff`: **the objectwise image of a morphism out of a
  finite free sheaf of modules is the span of the images of the tautological sections.** Both
  directions are `Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_freeMk`, over an arbitrary site.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.map_sectionOnRestriction`: **a section over `U`,
  read as a global section of `X|_U` and restricted to a smaller open, is the restriction of the
  original section.** `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionOnRestriction` carries
  a transport along `U.isOpenEmbedding.functor.obj ⊤ = U`, and this is the statement in which
  that transport disappears: it is discharged by substituting the equality of opens rather than
  rewritten, and what is left is that two morphisms of `Opens X` with the same source and target
  are equal.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_openSubspace_iff`:
  **the objectwise comparison.** Over an open `W ⊆ U` the image of the Koszul morphism of the
  `fᵢ` read on `X|_U` is the ideal generated by the restrictions of the `fᵢ`, which is the value
  over the corresponding object of `Opens X / U` of the span upstairs.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections`:
  **the hypothesis `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` consumes, for the Koszul
  morphism.** The sheaf of ideals generated on `X|_U` by the Koszul morphism and the sheaf of
  ideals generated on the slice site by `f₁, …, f_r` have the same sections over corresponding
  objects.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_koszulOpenSubspace`:
  the universal property of an exterior algebra crossing the identification of the two
  quotients, at the Koszul ideal — `Stacks.SheafOfModules`
  `.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_openSubspaceRingQuotient` with its hypothesis `hI'` discharged.

## Implementation notes

**Why the upstairs ideal is a span and not an `idealOfHom`.** The downstairs ideal is
`Stacks.Sites.idealOfHom` of a morphism out of `Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulFreeSheaf`, which
exists because `Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulHomOfSections` is stated for the site of opens of a
space. There is no such morphism on the slice site without first building a free sheaf of modules
there, and the free sheaf of modules is a sheafified coproduct, so that route would carry
sheafification hypotheses for the slice topology through every statement. Describing the ideal
upstairs by its span of sections avoids all of it, and loses nothing: what both
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` ask of the upstairs ideal is its sections.

**The two spellings of the structure sheaf of the slice.** As in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.QuotientRingSheafOpenSubspaceIdeal`, every sheaf of
rings is named once at the spelling its consumer demands —
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.sliceRingSheaf` for the slice structure sheaf and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRing` for the structure sheaf of `X|_U` — and nothing here
re-derives those spellings.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0942](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0942)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u v t m

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### The objectwise image of a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules -/

section FreeRange

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{t}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{t}]

/-- **The objectwise image of a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules is the span of
the images of the tautological sections.** Membership of a value of the morphism is the
coordinate formula `Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord`; conversely a tuple of
coefficients assembles into a section of the free sheaf by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeMk`, whose image is the corresponding combination. -/
theorem mem_range_app_free_iff {N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{t} R} {I : Type t} [Fintype I]
    [DecidableEq I] (p : _root_.SheafOfModules.free I ⟶ N) (V : Cᵒᵖ)
    (s : ToType (N.val.obj V)) :
    (∃ e, p.val.app V e = s) ↔
      ∃ a : I → ToType (R.obj.obj V), ∑ i, a i • (N.freeHomEquiv p i).eval V = s := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨e, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨freeCoord (S := R) V e, (app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord p V e).symm⟩
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨freeMk (S := R) V a, Eq.trans (app_freeMk p V a) ?_⟩
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => congrArg (a i • ·) (app_unitOne_ιFree_comp p i V)

end FreeRange

/-! ### The submodule generated by a finite family of sections -/

section Span

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}}

/-- **The submodule of a presheaf of modules generated, objectwise, by a finite family of its
sections.** Over an object of the site it is the span of the values of the family there; that
this is stable under restriction is the compatibility of the family, the restriction maps being
semilinear. -/
def spanSections (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) {I : Type*} [Fintype I] (s : I → M.sections) :
    M.Submodule where
  obj V := Submodule.span _ (Set.range fun i => (s i).eval V)
  map {V W} g := by
    intro x hx
    rw [Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun] at hx
    rw [Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun]
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
    refine ⟨fun i => R.map g (a i), ?_⟩
    rw [map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [map_smulₛₗ]
    exact congrArg (R.map g (a i) • ·) ((s i).property g).symm

/-- Membership in the submodule generated by a finite family of sections is being a linear
combination of its values. -/
theorem mem_spanSections_obj (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) {I : Type*} [Fintype I]
    (s : I → M.sections) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (x : ToType (M.obj V)) :
    x ∈ (spanSections M s).obj V ↔
      ∃ a : I → ToType (R.obj V), ∑ i, a i • (s i).eval V = x :=
  Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun _

end Span

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence

open Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {Y : TopCat.{u}} (Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) CommRingCat.{u})
  {r : ℕ} (g : Fin r → ↑(Osharp.obj.obj (op (⊤ : Opens ↥Y))))

/-- **The morphism attached to a sequence of global sections carries the `k`-th tautological
generator to the section obtained by restricting `g k` everywhere.** This is
`Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulHomOfSections` read through the universal property it is defined
by: `Stacks.RegularSequence.freeHomEquiv_koszulHomOfSections` gives its value over the whole
space, and a section of a presheaf of modules on a space is determined by that value
(`Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sections_ext_top`), which is why nothing has to be unfolded here. -/
theorem freeHomEquiv_koszulHomOfSections_eq (k : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
        (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp)).freeHomEquiv
      (koszulHomOfSections Osharp g) k =
      Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sectionOfTop _ (g k.down) :=
  Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sections_ext_top
    ((freeHomEquiv_koszulHomOfSections Osharp g k.down).trans
      (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sectionOfTop_val_top
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
          (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp)).val (g k.down)).symm)

/-- Linear combinations of two families with termwise equal members have the same values. -/
private theorem exists_sum_smul_eq_congr {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {A M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M]
    [SMul A M] {u v : ι → M} (h : ∀ i, u i = v i) (s : M) :
    (∃ a : ι → A, ∑ i, a i • u i = s) ↔ ∃ a : ι → A, ∑ i, a i • v i = s := by
  simp only [h]

/-- **The objectwise image of the Koszul morphism of a sequence of global sections is the ideal
generated by their restrictions.** This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_range_app_free_iff` at the morphism out of the free sheaf of modules
that `Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulHomOfSections` is, whose values on the tautological
generators are the sections themselves. -/
theorem mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_iff (V : (Opens ↥Y)ᵒᵖ)
    (s : ToType ((_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp)).val.obj V)) :
    (∃ e, (koszulHomOfSections Osharp g).val.app V e = s) ↔
      ∃ a : ULift.{u} (Fin r) →
          ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp).obj.obj V),
        ∑ k, a k • (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sectionOfTop
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
            (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp)).val (g k.down)).eval V = s := by
  classical
  refine Iff.trans (mem_range_app_free_iff (koszulHomOfSections Osharp g) V s) ?_
  exact exists_sum_smul_eq_congr (fun k => congrArg (fun t : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
    (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥Y) Osharp)).val.sections => t.eval V)
    (freeHomEquiv_koszulHomOfSections_eq Osharp g k)) s

end Stacks.RegularSequence

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

open Stacks.Sites Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.RegularSequence

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (U : Opens X.carrier)
  {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U))

/-- **A section over `U`, read as a global section of `X|_U` and restricted to a smaller open,
is the restriction of the original section.**
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionOnRestriction` transports along
`U.isOpenEmbedding.functor.obj ⊤ = U`, and the transport is discharged here by substituting that
equality of opens — not by rewriting under it — after which the two restriction morphisms have
the same source and target and `Opens X` is a partial order, so they are equal. -/
theorem map_sectionOnRestriction {B : Opens X.carrier}
    (ψ : B ⟶ U.isOpenEmbedding.functor.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥U)) (ψ' : B ⟶ U)
    (g : X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :
    X.presheaf.map ψ.op (sectionOnRestriction X U g) = X.presheaf.map ψ'.op g := by
  have key : ∀ (A : Opens X.carrier) (hA : A = U) (t : X.presheaf.obj (op A)),
      t = hA.symm ▸ g → ∀ χ : B ⟶ A,
        X.presheaf.map χ.op t = X.presheaf.map ψ'.op g := by
    intro A hA t ht χ
    subst hA
    subst ht
    rw [Subsingleton.elim χ ψ']
  exact key _ (Opens.isOpenEmbedding_obj_top U) _ rfl ψ

/-- **The family of sections of the slice structure sheaf `O_X|_U` given by `f₁, …, f_r`**: over
an object `W → U` of `Opens X / U` the restriction of `f k` along its structure morphism. -/
abbrev sliceSections (k : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val.sections :=
  mkOver (M := _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X)) (V := U) (f k.down)

/-- **The sheaf of ideals of the slice structure sheaf `O_X|_U` generated by `f₁, …, f_r`**: the
local closure of the objectwise span of their restrictions. This is the sheaf of ideals upstairs
that the identification of the two quotients of the structure sheaf over `U` consumes. -/
def sliceIdealOfSections : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (X.sheaf.over U) :=
  localClosure _ (spanSections (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val
    (sliceSections U f))

/-- **The section of the structure sheaf of `X|_U` determined by `f k` is the section of the
slice structure sheaf determined by `f k`.** The left-hand side restricts the reading of `f k`
as a global section of `X|_U`; the right-hand side restricts `f k` itself along the structure
morphism of the corresponding slice object. The two restrictions have the same source and
target once the transport in
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionOnRestriction` is discharged. -/
theorem eval_sectionOfTop_sectionOnRestriction (k : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) (V : Opens ↥U) :
    (Stacks.PresheafOfModules.sectionOfTop (Z := (openSubspace U).carrier)
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val
        (sectionOnRestriction X U (f k.down))).eval (op V) =
      (sliceSections U f k).eval (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V)) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (map_sectionOnRestriction U
    (homOfLE ((leOfHom ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V).hom).trans
      (Opens.isOpenEmbedding_obj_top U).ge))
    ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V).hom (f k.down))
  rfl

/-- **The objectwise comparison of the two images.** Over an open `W ⊆ U` a section of the
structure sheaf of `X|_U` lies in the image of the Koszul morphism of `f₁, …, f_r` exactly when
it is a combination of their restrictions — which is the value, over the corresponding object of
`Opens X / U`, of the span generated upstairs.

The image downstairs is computed by
`Stacks.RegularSequence.mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_iff`; the two resulting existential
statements then agree term by term, by `eval_sectionOfTop_sectionOnRestriction`. -/
theorem mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_openSubspace_iff (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
    (s : ToType ((_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val.obj V)) :
    (∃ e, (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace U).sheaf
        fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)).val.app V e = s) ↔
      s ∈ (spanSections (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val
        (sliceSections U f)).obj (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) := by
  refine Iff.trans (mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_iff (openSubspace U).sheaf
      (fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)) V s)
    (Iff.trans ?_ (mem_spanSections_obj
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val (sliceSections U f)
      (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) s).symm)
  exact exists_sum_smul_eq_congr (A := ToType ((openSubspaceRing U).obj.obj V))
    (eval_sectionOfTop_sectionOnRestriction U f · V.unop) s

/-- **The sheaf of ideals of the structure sheaf of `X|_U` that the local Koszul statements form
their quotient by**: the one generated by the Koszul morphism of `f₁, …, f_r` read there. This is
`Stacks.RegularSequence.quotientIdeal` at the structure sheaf of the open subspace, with its
site ascribed at the `↥U` spelling so that the local-surjectivity instance for its quotient map
is found. -/
abbrev koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (openSubspaceSheaf U) :=
  idealOfHom (O := openSubspaceSheaf U) (F := koszulFreeSheaf (openSubspace U).sheaf r)
    (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace U).sheaf fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j))

/-- **The hypothesis that the identification of the two quotients of the structure sheaf over
`U` consumes, for the Koszul morphism.** The sheaf of ideals generated on `X|_U` by the Koszul
morphism of `f₁, …, f_r` and the sheaf of ideals generated on the slice site by `f₁, …, f_r`
have the same sections over corresponding objects.

Both ideals are local closures, so the statement is not the objectwise one; what crosses the
site equivalence is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff`, fed with the
objectwise comparison `mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_openSubspace_iff`. -/
theorem sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ) :
    sectionIdeal (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f) V =
      sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
        (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) :=
  SetLike.ext fun s =>
    mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff U
      (spanSections (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val (sliceSections U f))
      (presheafRangeSubmodule
        (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace U).sheaf
          fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)).val)
      (fun W t => (mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_obj _ W t).trans
        (mem_range_koszulHomOfSections_openSubspace_iff U f W t))
      V s

/-! ### The descent transport at the Koszul ideal -/

variable [HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) CommRingCat.{u}]

open _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra in
/-- **The universal property of an exterior algebra crosses the identification of the two
quotients of the structure sheaf over `U`, at the Koszul ideal.** This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_openSubspaceRingQuotient` with its hypothesis
`hI'` discharged by `sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections`: the quotient formed on `X|_U`
is the one the local statements of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] use, and the quotient upstairs is by the
sheaf of ideals that `f₁, …, f_r` generate on the slice site. -/
theorem isExteriorAlgebra_descend_koszulOpenSubspace
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (openSubspaceRing U))
    (hA : ∀ (n : ℤ) (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ) (b : (openSubspaceRing U).obj.obj V),
      b ∈ RingHom.ker ((quotientRingHom (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)).hom.app V).hom →
        ∀ m : (A.piece n).val.obj V, b • m = 0)
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (openSubspaceRingSheaf U (R' := toRingCat ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U)
        (quotientRingSheaf.{u, u, u} (sliceIdealOfSections U f))))}
    {ι : M ⟶ (descend (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom (sliceIdealOfSections U f))) A
      (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
        (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
        (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f) A hA)).piece 1}
    (h : IsExteriorAlgebra (descend (quotientRingHom (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)) A hA)
      (genScalarRestrict (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
          (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
          (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f)) ι ≫
        (descendRingIsoHom (quotientRingHom (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f))
          (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom (sliceIdealOfSections U f)))
          (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
            (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
            (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f))
          (quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom' U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
            (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
            (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f)) A hA
          (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
            (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
            (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f) A hA)).app 1)) :
    IsExteriorAlgebra
      (descend (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom (sliceIdealOfSections U f))) A
        (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
          (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f)
          (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f) A hA)) ι :=
  isExteriorAlgebra_descend_openSubspaceRingQuotient U (sliceIdealOfSections U f)
    (koszulOpenSubspaceIdeal U f) (sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_koszulHomOfSections U f) A hA h

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
